Text:
The Reconciliator makes the desk start one program when a person opens a file with one of some extensions.
A 'program' is named by the TaggedText that encodes the path of that program.
os.holders is a Holders: (OSExtension->TaggedText) is in os.holders exactly while the desk starts the program TaggedText when a person opens a file with the extension OSExtension, for example with a double click.
The desk, a person and every program can change os.holders at any moment.
//later: how reconciliator$personAllows asks a person, and which program shows the question of reconciliator$personAllows
//later: what the Reconciliator writes on each desk, and how the Reconciliator reads os.holders on each desk
//later: the icons that the desk shows for the files of an extension and for the windows of a program
//later: two calls of reconciliator$reconcile never run at the same time on one desk

Grammar:
OSExtensions ::= OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn
FearlessExtension ::= "fearless" | "fapp" [0-9][0-9][0-9] | "ffile" [0-9][0-9][0-9]
Holders ::= Holder1 .. Holdern
Holder ::= (OSExtension->TaggedText)

Well formedness:
in OSExtensions: if OSExtensions is OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn, then OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn are disjoint
in Holders: if Holders is (OSExtension1->_) .. (OSExtensionn->_), then OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn are disjoint

Notation: Holders.mustAsk(TaggedText,OSExtension,TaggedText') where:
- (OSExtension->TaggedText') in Holders
- the last segment of the path that TaggedText' encodes is not the last segment of the path that TaggedText encodes
- OSExtension is not of form FearlessExtension

Signature: reconciliator$personAllows(TaggedText,OSExtension,TaggedText')//holds when a person, asked, lets the program TaggedText replace the program TaggedText' for the files with the extension OSExtension

Signature: reconciliator$allowed(TaggedText,OSExtensions) = OSExtensions'

Define OSExtension in reconciliator$allowed(TaggedText,OSExtensions):
A fact OSExtension in OSExtensions
B fact not os.holders.mustAsk(TaggedText,OSExtension,_)

Define OSExtension in reconciliator$allowed(TaggedText,OSExtensions):
A fact OSExtension in OSExtensions
B fact os.holders.mustAsk(TaggedText,OSExtension,TaggedText')
C fact reconciliator$personAllows(TaggedText,OSExtension,TaggedText')

Define reconciliator$reconcile(TaggedText,OSExtensions):
A fact reconciliator$allowed(TaggedText,OSExtensions) = OSExtension1 .. OSExtensionn
B action the desk is changed so that (OSExtension1->TaggedText) .. (OSExtensionn->TaggedText) are in os.holders; the Holder of every other OSExtension stays as it is
C if OSExtensioni is of form FearlessExtension and (OSExtensioni->TaggedText) is not in os.holders, error reconciliatorErrorFearlessExtensionIsNotHeld(OSExtensioni)

Implementation notes:
In Define reconciliator$reconcile, when the condition of line C holds, the implementation does line B again. The error of line C happens when that condition still holds after line B was done 3 times.
